'''Valin Halcyon''' was an individual whose name was carved on the wall of a [[Mapuzo safehouse|safehouse]] on the [[planet]] [[Mapuzo]] that was part of the [[Hidden Path]], a network of safe houses that smuggled [[Force-sensitive]]s and [[Jedi]] away from the [[Galactic Empire]] and to the planet [[Jabiim]] to get new identities and be protected. [[Jedi Master]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] saw their name among others on the wall when he and [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] were smuggled in by [[Tala Durith]]<ref name="Part III">{{Kenobi|Part III}}</ref> in [[9 BBY]].<ref name="Timeline">{{SW|url=news/future-lucasfilm-projects-revealed|text=Future Lucasfilm Projects Revealed}} states that ''Obi-Wan Kenobi'' is set ten [[Standard year|years]] after the events of [[Star Wars: Episode III Revenge of the Sith|''Star Wars'': Episode III ''Revenge of the Sith'']], which ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates to [[19 BBY]]. Therefore, ''Obi-Wan Kenobi'' must be set in [[9 BBY]].</ref> The same name was carved into a wall at the Path's base on Jabiim, at least three times.<ref name="Part V">{{Kenobi|Part V}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:HalHorn.jpg|200px|thumb|Valin Halcyon in the ''Star Wars'' Legends continuity]]
Valin Halcyon was first [[canon]]ically mentioned, in [[Aurebesh]] script, in "[[Part III]]" of the television series [[Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi|''Obi-Wan Kenobi'']],<ref name="Part III" /> which premiered on [[Disney+]] on [[June 1]], [[2022]].<ref name="D23">{{D23|url=everything-new-you-can-stream-on-disney-in-june-2022|text=Everything New You Can Stream on Disney+ in June 2022}}</ref> In the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, [[Hal Horn]],<ref name="Rogue Squadron">''[[X-Wing: Rogue Squadron]]''</ref> born Valin Halcyon, was a [[Corellian/Legends|Corellian]] [[Jedi/Legends|Jedi]] survivor<ref name="The Krytos Trap">''[[X-Wing: The Krytos Trap]]''</ref> and member of the [[Corellian Security Force]].<ref name="Rogue Squadron" /> [[Gender/Legends|He]] was first mentioned in [[Michael A. Stackpole]]'s [[1996]] novel ''[[X-Wing: Rogue Squadron]]'', the first novel in the [[Star Wars: X-Wing (novel series)|''Star Wars: X-Wing'']] novel series,<ref name="Rogue Squadron" /> and first appeared in Stackpole and [[Timothy Zahn]]'s [[1997]] short story ''[[Side Trip]]'', first published in the [[Star Wars Adventure Journal 12|twelfth issue]] of ''[[Star Wars Adventure Journal]]''.<ref name="Side Trip">"[[Side Trip]]"</ref>

